\title{Calling convention}
\date{2026-07-05T22:23:03Z}

\p{The way that the variables are stored and the parameters and return values are transferred by the computer}

\remark{
The most common calling convention is as defined in the [System V ABI](https://wiki.osdev.org/System_V_ABI#x86-64).
}

\remark{
Assembly language can use whatever calling convention you want.
}
